        "name": "pc-check-flag",
        "description": "Pure-logic validator that returns whether a raw candidate value is exactly a boolean. Raw inputs may omit flag or hold any JSON value. Only the exact booleans True and False are valid; any other value, a missing flag, or null is invalid. Returns {valid: boolean, flag: original value if valid else null}. No imports, I/O, host calls, exceptions or type coercion. The helper is defined and invoked at module scope to assign result.",
        "content": "def is_exact_flag(value):\n    return isinstance(value, bool)\nresult = {\"valid\": is_exact_flag(inputs.get(\"flag\")), \"flag\": inputs.get(\"flag\") if is_exact_flag(inputs.get(\"flag\")) else None}"
      }
    }
  ],
  "composition_summary": "Offline-design mode. Drafted one class-22 PythonCode component named pc-check-flag with name/description/content only. The body is pure logic: a helper is_exact_flag returns isinstance(value, bool), and module scope invokes it twice to assign result = {valid, flag} where flag is the original value only when valid else null. No imports, I/O, host calls, exceptions or coercion. Typed inputs are a target interface, not deployed runtime support; the draft remains unapproved with no tests/submission/approval claims.",
